h bank is the remains of Union Mills Lock.","","","w1341433500"],["Crofton Lock","ruins","The remains of wood framing and planking backed by thick stonewalls are visible on the river bottom when the river is low.","","","w1341433499"],["Broken Island Locks and Dam","ruins","Stone and timbers in the riverbed are the remains of the 1830's lock and dam.","","","w1341433497"],["Palmyra Mill Lock","ruins","Ruins of the lock, a mill, and the piers from a burned down covered bridge are all in this area.","","","w1341433496"],["Strange's Lock","ruins","Strange's Lock. Built for batteau boats around the 1830's. The wooden sides of the lock have been preserved at the water level.","","","w1341433473"],["Carysbrook Lock and Dam","ruins","Built during the 1850's. The stone lock and traces of the dam still exist here.","","","w1341433476"],["White Rock Lock and Dam","ruins","Built in the 1920's. The lock's stone wall remains standing on the east bank. The crib dam has been reduces to rubble and creates the rapids found in this area.","","","w1341433477"],["Rivanna Mills Dam","ruins","Remains of a 19-foot high dam dating from the 1850's. On the north side of the river is the remains of the basement wall of the old flour mill.","","","w1341433481"],["Bridge piers at Bryant's Ford","ruins","Rock remains of bridge piers at Bryant's Ford.","","","w1341433483"],["Wood's Mill Dam","ruins","The remains of Wood's Mill Dam form the rapids here.","","","w1341433493"],["Columbia Junction Lock","ruins","Built in the 1830's this lock was unique in that it had gates facing opposite directions to be able to seal off water from either the Rivanna connexion or Kanawha canals. One of the lock's stone walls is still visible on the south side of the river.","","","w1341433494"],["Historical plaque","plaque","","","","n13858780714"],["Historical plaque","plaque","Frances Broaddus-Crutchfield Order of the Arrow Pavilion Dedicated September 14, 2019 OA Vigil Honor Member Founder's Award - Silver Beaver